        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://crawfordcopa.com/history/boro/blooming"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough incorporated on May 17, 1867, emerging from Woodcock Township in Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://crawfordcopa.com/history/boro/blooming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Blooming Valley sits on the divide between Blooming Valley Run and Sugar Creek, whose waters flow to French Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blooming_Valley%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pennsylvania Routes 77 and 198 cross in the town center, linking it to Meadville and Saegertown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blooming_Valley%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area’s elevation ranges from 1,219 to 1,530 feet, giving gentle hills around the borough.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blooming_Valley%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Crawford County, where Blooming Valley lies, was named for Colonel William Crawford, a defender of settlers.",
